      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): close transport before gateway teardown",
        "body": "Closes #106005\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nQA Smoke scenarios can finish successfully while Crabline transport work is still delivering an HTTP response. The suite stopped the gateway first, so that in-flight delivery became an unhandled `HTTP response closed before delivery completed` rejection.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nClose the transport before stopping the gateway. Transport cleanup drains outstanding provider HTTP work while the gateway can still accept delivery. The cleanup-order regression test preserves that ordering even when cleanup reports an error.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA Smoke no longer reports a post-success unhandled rejection caused by its own teardown order. Runtime behavior outside QA Lab is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact-head focused QA extension suite on `fd41dc3f1c600cd948e37f97a2078122ebde868b`: 29 passed.\n- Exact-head QA smoke on the QA Lab gateway plus `qa-channel` transport: `channel-chat-baseline` passed 1/1; the captured output reached `CRABBOX_PHASE:complete` and explicitly confirmed `TEARDOWN_REJECTION:absent`.\n- Remote proof ran from a fresh detached checkout using DigitalOcean Crabbox (`provider=digitalocean`, lease `cbx_ff0b1c157c92`, public networking, Tailscale disabled); the lease was deleted after validation.\n- Formatting and type-aware OXLint passed for the two changed files.\n- Fresh autoreview found no in-scope actionable findings.\n- Current main's `d9623bd46f` owns the previously failing Crabline fixture/type-contract update; this PR intentionally contains only teardown ordering and its regression test.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe full extension test-type project was not green locally because current main had unrelated iMessage nullability errors during the initial repair. The exact-head remote proof above covers this PR's changed behavior.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. No agent transcript attached (not requested).\n",
